_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 15
---
order: 15
---
short_label: VII.15
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If a unit number measures any number, and another number measures any other number the same number of times, then alternately, the unit measures the third number the same number of times that the second measures the fourth.
----
proof:

Let the unit {A} measure any number {BC}, and let another number {D} measure any other number {EF} the same number of times.

I say that, alternately also, the unit measures the number {D} the same number of times that {BC} measures {EF}.

